% \end{equation}\\

The final ancillary qubit is a single qubit initialised in a $\ket{0}$ state. This qubit's amplitude encodes the mean payoff of the option and hence can be measured to determine the final Option Price. Amplitude estimation techniques outlined by previous works on QAMC can then be used to achieve quadratic speed up.





