\title[Isaacs type results for fusion categories]
{On some integral properties of %Frobenius-Perron 
dimensions in Isaacs fusion categories}

\begin{abstract}
For a fusion category, we prove some new integral properties concerning the dimension of a simple object that generates a Isaacs fusion subcategory. If any such fusion subcategory is Isaacs this implies that $\cc$ is a Frobenius type fusion category. A stronger divisibility result is proven for any modular fusion category. This divisibility result implies the  converse direction of a Ito-Michler type result for modular fusion categories,  see \cite[Proposition 2.3]{b-conj-im}. 
\end{abstract}


