\includegraphics[width=10cm]{CNOT_rearrange.pdf}
	\caption{
    This figure explains the final line in \eqref{eq:CNOT_rearrange} visually for $\ell=3$. Each arrow indicates the action of a CNOT gate. 
    Acting these operations to $\prod_{a=1}^8\ket{n_a}_a$, we turn the 8-th qubit to be in the state $\ket{n_1\oplus\cdots\oplus n_8}_8$. 
    While $2^\ell-1=7$ CNOT gates are needed, the depth is $\ell=3$. 
