\begin{abstract}
We compute the $E_2$ page in the Rasmussen spectral sequence from triply graded to $\fgl_N$ Khovanov--Rozansky stable homology of torus knots. This confirms a weak form of the conjecture of the second author, Oblomkov, and Rasmussen. The main tool is the link-splitting deformation, or $y$-ification, of link homology; in the $y$-ified context, the relevant Rasmussen spectral sequence collapses and we explicitly compute the $y$-ified $\fgl_N$ stable Khovanov--Rozansky homology of torus knots for all $N$.
\end{abstract}


\maketitle
