\subsubsection{Primitives}

Most LLM-based multi-agent Agentic frameworks make use of ``primitives'' that abstract low-level control into multi-step routines. For example, upon calling \texttt{move to location}, the agent will take multiple steps to reach the target by repeating the path-finding algorithms. These primitives can reduce token usage and simplify reasoning by treating the system as a hierarchical control framework. All primitives are listed in the Appendix.

