\ar[r]&0\\ 0\ar[r]& M\ar[r]^{u} & P \ar[r]\ar[d] & L\ar[r]\ar[d]&0\\ && 0&0}\]}Since $\Gp(R)$ is closed under extensions,   the right-hand column implies that $C\in\Gp(R)$, and so, the upper row is the desired sequence.
