\section{\label{sec3}Numerical findings of four-wing attractor}

Before we present the geometrical properties, based on the Nambu mechanics, we present here the direct numerical result of phase space portrait and other properties like bifurcation, Lyapunov exponent etc. for comparison purpose.

The dynamical equations of Four-wing attractor are given by 
\begin{equation}\label{eq1}
	\begin{cases}
		\dot{x} =ax+cyz \\
		\dot{y}=bx+dy-xz \\
		\dot{z}=ez+fxy 
	\end{cases}\,.
\end{equation}

where $a$, $b$, $c$, $d$, $e$, and $f$ are different parameters. The system shows four-wing chaotic dynamics for the values, $a=0.2$, $b=-0.01$, $c=1$, $d=-0.4$, $e=-1$, $f=-1$.




The system's dynamical behavior (\ref{eq1}) is numerically analyzed using the standard fourth-order Runge–Kutta algorithm with a constant stepsize of 0.001. In addition to this, Lyapunov exponents are computed numerically with the help of Gram-Schmidt orthonormalization \cite{christiansen1997computing}. Various phase portraits are shown in the FIG.\ref{fig1}. 

