The initial values of the system are prescribed on the closed intersecting trajectory of the Nambu surfaces. As far as the topology is concerned, each and every geometrical shape is associated with some energy. Hence, the parent Nambu surfaces are also associated with some energy. It means both the upper and lower halves expansion of the hyperboloid surface and the radius of cylinder depict their corresponding energies associated with these geometrical shapes. The energy is quantified by the initial conditions. %\bf{For example, if  the radius of cylinder is small for certain initial condition, the energy of that cylindrical surface is also small. In that case it is considered to be a stable at that particular instant. Similarly, the energy of that cylindrical surface will be considered very high and of course that geometrical shape may be a unstable surface for a particular instant when the associated initial condition will generate a large radius cylinder.}
