%\subsubsection*{Threshold property}
\noindent
\\ \textbf{Threshold property:} The threshold property is one of the major attributes that should characterise a spiking neuron; this is typically observed as an-all-non response to an expernal perturbation or stimulus input. This means that the system either responds in the form of an excursion/output when the stimulus/input is sufficiently strong or remains non responsive and in its initial state potential when the stimulus/input is not sufficiently strong.
