\subsection{Definition of Bias}
Bias, in a broad sense, encompasses various phenomena tied to cognition, conflicts of interest, statistical variations, and prejudices, depending on the context \cite{WikipediaBias}. In machine learning (ML), bias refers to the unequal error rates produced by a model for specific speaker groups based on personal attributes, like, age, language, accent, health, country of origin. In ASR, bias referred to in literature, is generally a `performance difference' or `performance disparity' of error rates between speaker groups. Addressing these disparities is crucial for mitigating bias and promoting fairness in speech recognition systems \cite{Dheram2022TowardDisparities,feng2021quantifying}.

