\section{Conclusion}
The error rate is a fundamental metric offering a holistic system evaluation, however, our granular, intersectional analysis of  different demographic speaker groups showed that error rate does not reflect the performance and bias within and across speaker groups well. In line with the potential pitfalls, there is a clear need for performance and bias measures to capture performance variation, and this paper gives recommendations on it. %Unlike WER, there is no ground-truth in bias (only human judgement), hence, user feedback and experiences should be considered for qualitative insights into the real-world impact of bias, until a metric with joint performance and bias assessment is explored in the future.




