In this subsection, we analyze the stability regions of the second high-order one-step scheme \eqref{eq13}. Considering the multiplicity of involved parameters, we choose to fix the value of $\beta_3$ to streamline the analysis.

For the test equation $u_t=\lambda u$, the proposed scheme \eqref{eq13} reduces to the following
\begin{equation}
\begin{aligned}
&\left[(-\beta_1\lambda\Delta t+1)(-\beta_2\lambda\Delta t+1)(-\beta_3\lambda\Delta t+1)-(\beta_1+\beta_2+\beta_3)\lambda\Delta t+5\right]u^{n+1}\\
=&[-(\beta_1-1)\lambda\Delta t+1][-(\beta_2-1)\lambda\Delta t+1][-(\beta_3-1)\lambda\Delta t+1]u^n \\
&+[-(\beta_1+\beta_2+\beta_3-3)\lambda\Delta t+5]u^n.
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}

