\section{Concluding remarks}
In this paper, we construct a series of high-order one-step schemes for parabolic equations and rigorously prove that these schemes achieve A-stability and even L-stability under specified parameter selections. Furthermore, we demonstrate that the proposed one-step schemes constitutes an effective extension of classical one-step Runge-Kutta methods. Numerical experiments conclusively validate that the new schemes attain broader stability regions than RK methods and exhibit enhanced computational efficacy across diverse parabolic problems.

