\end{figure}

The peculiar decay properties of the high-spin ground state of $^{257}$Db have also been confronted with Geant4 Monte Carlo simulations, leading to a new spin and parity assignment. The implications for the sequence of proton states above $Z$~=~100 and the relative position of high-$j$ shells are discussed. 

