The measured widths for the two peaks of $^{253}$Lr, shown in Fig.~\ref{Ea_Lr}, as well as the sharp peak of the low-spin state $\alpha$-decay of $^{257}$Db, are comparable to the experimental resolution. These measured widths characteristics, along with the non-observation of $\gamma$ rays or Internal Conversion Electrons (ICEs) in coincidence, suggests that these decays exhibit minimal fine structure.
